- How would you adapt this for non-uniform distributions or dynamic M?
- How does the choice of S affect query latency in a high-throughput system?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of streaming complexity with fixed memory, practical heavy-hitter detection, and batch-based processing.

## Key Concepts
- Misra-Gries heavy-hitter algorithm
- Amortized vs per-item cost
- Threshold guarantees with finite counters
- Secondary verification for exact counts

## Code Example
```javascript
class MG {
  constructor(H){ this.H=H; this.counters=new Map(); }
  update(x){
    if (this.counters.has(x)) this.counters.set(x, this.counters.get(x)+1);
    else if (this.counters.size < this.H) this.counters.set(x,1);
    else {
      for (let k of Array.from(this.counters.keys())) {
        this.counters.set(k, this.counters.get(k)-1);
        if (this.counters.get(k)===0) this.counters.delete(k);
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests streaming algorithm intuition and amortized reasoning. Detecting heavy hitters with bounded memory on a growing stream is a common interview topic; Misra–Gries provides deterministic guarantees with simple updates.

## Key Concepts
- Misra–Gries heavy-hitters
- Choice of k = floor(1/phi) + 1 to bound missed items
- Amortized O(1) per element, O(k) memory
- Trade-offs: larger k reduces false positives but uses more memory

## Code Example
```javascript
class MGHeavyHitters {
  constructor(k) {
    this.k = k;
    this.counters = new Map();
  }
  update(x) {
    if (this.counters.has(x)) {
      this.counters.set(x, this.counters.get(x) + 1);
      return;
    }
    if (this.counters.size < this.k) {
      this.counters.set(x, 1);
      return;
    }
    for (const [key, val] of Array.from(this.counters)) {
      if (val === 1) this.counters.delete(key);
      else this.counters.set(key, val - 1);
    }
  }
  candidates() { return Array.from(this.counters.keys()); }
}
```

